  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Oregon are concentrated and much lower so far in FY2027 compared with prior full fiscal years. Oregon recorded $82.9M in obligations across 997 awards in FY2027 to date. The average award size was $83.2K and obligations fell 96.8% year over year. By comparison, Oregon obligations were $2.6B in FY26, $2.2B in FY25, $2.6B in FY24, $2.7B in FY23, and $1.9B in FY22. The Department of Agriculture, Department of Veterans Affairs, and Department of Justice are the top buying agencies in FY2027 to date. Support Activities for Forestry, Other Computer Related Services, and Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction are the largest industries by obligations. The vendor list is led by M.J. HUGHES CONSTRUCTION, INC., BAHFED CORP, and METRO WEST AMBULANCE SERVICE, INC. This snapshot reflects partial-year totals for FY2027 and shows how spending so far differs from recent full-year patterns.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why are FY2027 obligations so low compared with recent years?",
        "body": "Year-to-date reporting shows $82.9M in obligations for FY2027 to date while prior full years were in the billions. Fiscal year totals for FY26 through FY22 ranged from $1.9B to $2.7B, so current-year totals are partial and not directly comparable. The year-over-year change is down 96.8%, which reflects the partial nature of FY2027 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries dominate FY2027 federal contracting in Oregon?",
        "body": "The Department of Agriculture obligated $35.6M in FY2027 to date, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $21M and the Department of Justice with $7.1M. Support Activities for Forestry is the largest industry with $17.9M, followed by Other Computer Related Services with $5.6M and Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction with $4.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
